Z||000000||Don_Chi_Chi||10-23-2001||01:05 PM||||Kay, so I just bought a Ghetto Blaster that plays Mp3 CD's and now I wanna make some.  Do I need to make a playlist and put it on the CD to?  How do you seperate albums on the CDs and stuff?  And specific (preferably freeware) programs that work best for this kinda thing?<P>------------------<BR>Previously known as Saleenfiero||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||10-23-2001||02:01 PM||||For the software, get a program called Nero.  You should be able to get it at download.com.<P>As far as your playlist/file separation stuff, that's kind of the downfall with most current mp3 cd players...they don't have that.  The ones I've seen in person just have a regular CD with a ton of tracks basically; they didn't have any extra functions that allowed a playlist or the ability to separate stuff into folders.  I'm sure this will come, in good time.  Personally it's not that big of a deal for me, because I like all kinds of music; if I don't happen to like that song I'm listening to at that point in time, I'm not above hitting the track forward button a few times <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>By the way, what is a Ghetto Blaster?  And what brand did you get(cost?)?  I've been eyeballing the Aiwa mp3 cd player..they're on ebay for 200 bucks consistently!  I just need to figure out my wiring problem I have currently... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Don_Chi_Chi||10-23-2001||06:24 PM||||Hey am I the only one who still calls little home stereos ghetto blasters?  Thanx for the help Nash, I don't know what make/model my stereo is, but it did say that you could have track lists and album names and stuff so I just decided to ask.<P>------------------<BR>Previously known as Saleenfiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-24-2001||05:49 AM||||"Ghetto Blaster" is the same as a "boom box", right?  Stereo and speakers all in one with a handle on top?  That's what I used to call 'em until everyone got all up in arms about everything being PC.  Now we have to call them "compact, portable, self-contained stereos".||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||10-24-2001||11:18 AM||||Oh, I get it..it's a boom box.  I've never heard that..I must not be hip <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Perhaps it has the ability to make track lists and program names into it ON the player, but not on the cd.  Didn't it come with an instruction booklet? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Don_Chi_Chi||10-24-2001||12:12 PM||||No it can't name CD's on it, but it will allow folders to seperate albums and stuff.  And yeah, I got an instruction manual, but as with most of them these days the company is more worried about you registering the purchase that any instructions.<BR>I've been encountering a new problem.  Every time I try to make an mp3 CD and then put in in my stereo, it will skip like 5 seconds at the beginning of every track.  These are brand new CD's and a brand new computer recording so its gotta either be the cheap mp3 stereo I have or the my recording methods.  Anyone got any ideas?  Do mp3 stereos need a few seconds to build up a cache of info or something?<P>------------------<BR>Previously known as Saleenfiero||||reg||1
